---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy" lang="en" description="How LISA Cloud and local Mac mode process accounts, conversations, and AI requests.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="rule"></span> PRIVACY <b>· updated 2026-09-28</b></p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      LISA is a personal AI assistant with two modes: <strong>LISA Cloud</strong>, operated
      by us, and a backend on <strong>your own Mac</strong>. Cloud mode processes and stores
      your account and assistant data. Local mode uses the server and AI providers you choose.
      We do not sell your personal data or use advertising tracking SDKs.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="highlight">
    <p class="eyebrow"><b>What we collect</b></p>
    <p class="big">Local mode: nothing — to us.</p>
    <p>
      Lisa Pocket and Lisa collect no analytics, no advertising identifiers, and contain no
      third-party tracking SDKs. Local mode does not require a LISA Cloud account. If you opt into a <strong>LISA Cloud account</strong>, we hold exactly
      what the section below lists — your email, your sign-in identifier, and your Lisa's
      data. You can request account deletion within the app.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="policy">
    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>What stays on your device</b></p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Connection settings</strong> — the address of your backend and a device
          token are stored on your device (the iOS Keychain / app preferences) so the app can
          reconnect. The connection token is sent only to the backend it authenticates, including
          LISA Cloud when you choose cloud mode.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your conversations and Lisa’s memory (“soul”)</strong> live on the backend
          you connect to — your own Mac (under <code>~/.lisa</code>) or a Lisa Cloud instance
          you use. The app is a window onto that backend.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>Your backend &amp; LLM providers</b></p>
      <p>
        LISA Cloud sends your message, relevant conversation history, assistant memory,
        and tool results to <strong>Google Gemini</strong> to generate your response. This
        can include personal information you put in those materials. We use Gemini API
        through a Google Cloud project with active billing. Under Google's
        <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/terms">paid-service terms</a>, prompts and
        responses are not used to improve Google's products. Google may retain them for
        a limited period for abuse prevention, security, or legal requirements, and may
        process them in countries where Google or its agents have facilities.
      </p>
      <p>
        Third parties we engage to process personal data must provide the same or equal
        protection as this policy, including limited-purpose processing, confidentiality,
        security, and applicable deletion obligations. Google's
        <a href="https://business.safety.google/processorterms/">Data Processing Addendum</a>
        applies to paid Gemini prompts and responses. Service and billing metadata are
        also processed under Google's applicable privacy and data-protection terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        With your own Mac, you choose the server and AI provider (for example Anthropic,
        OpenAI, Google, or Zhipu/GLM); review that provider's terms and settings before use.
        Those independently configured services are not operated by us. A local model can
        keep inference on your Mac; connecting a Mac alone does not keep remote inference
        on your device.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>Consent and withdrawal in Lisa Pocket</b></p>
      <p>
        Before sending a chat message, the iOS app identifies the configured AI recipients,
        explains the data involved, and asks for your explicit permission. Cancel leaves
        the draft unsent. Consent is limited to the current app session and connection;
        a changed recipient requires permission again. In <strong>Settings → AI data
        sharing → Withdraw AI consent</strong>, you can stop an active chat request and
        require fresh permission before future messages from this app. Withdrawal cannot
        recall information already processed and does not erase your history. It does not
        disable independent automations on your Mac; stop those on your own server.
        Use account deletion below, or contact us privately, to request deletion.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>LISA Cloud accounts (optional)</b></p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>What we store</strong> — your email address, a sign-in identifier
          (Apple/Google <code>sub</code> or a password hash — never the password itself), and
          your Lisa's per-account home: her soul, your conversations, and anything you add to
          her knowledge base. We also encrypt and store the Apple authorization token when supplied,
          so we can revoke that authorization when you delete your account.
          Stored on Google Cloud (us-central1), isolated per account.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What we process</strong> — chat messages pass through the account's metered
          LLM provider to answer you; token counts are metered for billing. We keep an
          append-only usage ledger (model, token counts, cost) — not message content.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Service providers</strong> — Google Cloud (hosting and storage), Google Gemini (AI inference),
          Resend (verification &amp; sign-in code emails), Stripe (web top-ups), Apple
          (Sign in with Apple, iOS purchases), Google (Sign in with Google), Cloudflare
          (bot-check on signup). These services receive only the data needed for their
          function, such as an email address for a sign-in email, an account identifier
          for authentication, or transaction identifiers and purchase receipts for credits.
          We do not receive your full payment card details from Apple or Stripe.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Operational data</strong> — service logs can include request IP addresses,
          times, routes, response status, errors, and account or transaction identifiers.
          We use these to operate the service, prevent abuse, and diagnose failures, not
          for advertising or cross-app tracking. We retain account data until you delete
          it; operational, payment, and provider records are kept as needed for security,
          accounting, dispute handling, and legal obligations.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Deletion</strong> — "Delete account" in the app removes the account record
          and wipes the per-account home entirely; every session is invalidated at that
          instant. Payment transaction records used for deduplication and refunds are separate
          from conversation storage. For Apple sign-ins with a saved authorization token,
          deletion also revokes that authorization. For an earlier sign-in without a saved token,
          we delete the Lisa data and show Apple's instructions for removing the remaining Apple connection. Provider-side records
          and infrastructure backups follow
          their respective retention policies; contact us for a data request.
        </li>
        <li>
          The App Review demonstration account is shared with reviewers. Do not place personal
          information in that account. Ordinary cloud accounts have separate assistant data.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>Notifications</b></p>
      <p>
        If you enable push notifications, a push token (Apple APNs, or an ntfy topic you choose)
        is used <em>only</em> to deliver the alerts you opt into, routed through the backend you
        paired with. It is not used for tracking.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>Age requirement</b></p>
      <p>LISA is intended for adults aged 18 or older. Lisa Pocket requires confirmation
        before enabling AI chat. Do not use the service if you are under 18. If we learn
        that we hold a minor's personal data, we will take steps to delete it; please
        contact us privately using the email below.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>Changes</b></p>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the apps evolve; material changes will be noted here with a
        new date. The source is public:
        <a href="https://github.com/oratis/LISA">github.com/oratis/LISA</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>Contact</b></p>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy? Open an issue at
        <a href="https://github.com/oratis/LISA/issues">github.com/oratis/LISA/issues</a>
        or email <a href="mailto:wangharp@gmail.com">wangharp@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <style>
    .page-head h1 { margin-bottom: .4rem; }
    .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--muted); max-width: 68ch; }

    .highlight {
      margin: 2.2rem 0 0; background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--panel), var(--bg-elev));
      border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 3px solid var(--good);
      border-radius: 14px; padding: 1.3rem 1.5rem;
    }
    .highlight .eyebrow { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
    .highlight .big {
      font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.55rem;
      color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 .5rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }
    .highlight p:last-child { margin: 0; max-width: 70ch; }

    .policy { display: grid; gap: 2rem; margin-top: 2.2rem; }
    .pol .eyebrow { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
    .pol p { margin: 0; max-width: 72ch; }
    .pol p + p { margin-top: .9rem; }
    .pol ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; max-width: 72ch; }
    .pol li { margin: .5rem 0; color: var(--muted); }
    .pol li strong { color: var(--ink); }
  </style>
</Base>
